{"term":"extinct","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e6c9c8ba378750dc45","definition":"Of fire, etc.: no longer alight; of a light, etc.: no longer shining; extinguished, quenched.","example":"Edward’s cigarillo was extinct by the time he had finished talking.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["alight","burning"],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic, not-comparable","register":"archaic, not-comparable","wordFamily":["coextinct","extinctic","extinct language","extinctness","extinctor","extinctual","extincture","inextinct","nonextinct","pseudoextinct","semiextinct","unextinct"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extinct#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:776d69c85aefff08aa","definition":"Of feelings, a person's spirit, a state of affairs, etc.: put out, as if like a fire; quenched, suppressed.","example":"My breath is corrupt, my dayes are extinct, the graues are ready for me.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, not-comparable","register":"figuratively, not-comparable","wordFamily":["coextinct","extinctic","extinct language","extinctness","extinctor","extinctual","extincture","inextinct","nonextinct","pseudoextinct","semiextinct","unextinct"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extinct#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8860ef278c34fedbb6","definition":"Of customs, ideas, laws and legal rights, offices, organizations, languages, etc.: no longer existing or in use; defunct, discontinued, obsolete; specifically, of a title of nobility: no longer having any person qualified to hold it.","example":"Luckily, such ideas about race are extinct in current sociological theory.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["anachronistic","antediluvial","antediluvian","antiquated","antique","archaic","backward","backwards","behind the